{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-311a-7369-b2b8-a9951cb6b024","id":"01a1a5f9-ccf4-74de-9609-263a72e5a888","idempotency_key":"6d8cfd0a26af52e37e0a47bfd79fe2b754e6dde2b16d1b6f640e6e5b5ebc0dc6","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T09:52:54Z","payload":{"note":"crates/ai/tests/common/mod.rs is a MockServer: a real HTTP endpoint on 127.0.0.1 with an OS-chosen port, answering JSON, chunked text/event-stream, 429, 500, a hang (so the client's own timeout fires) or a dropped socket, and recording every request body. crates/ai/tests/runtime_mock.rs drives the real OpenAiProvider over it: a plain completion (asserting the request carried model and messages), a streamed one arriving as several ContentDeltas, reasoning travelling with the answer, 429 -> provider_rate_limited (retryable), 500 -> provider_server_error, an unanswered request -> provider_timeout with a 400ms budget, a dropped connection -> a network/protocol error rather than a panic, a tool call parsed with its arguments (play_move with board_id/move/expected_revision), and an illegal move corrected over the wire (two requests, the retry carrying 'not a legal move'). No live network: the fixture binds loopback and the test asserts the URL is 127.0.0.1 on a non-privileged port. 10 tests, and 'cargo test -p rbc-ai --all-features runtime_mock' is the single command.","target":"t-7a66"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
